{"story_id":61818,"updated_at":"2026-11-05T23:11:08","headline_en":"Maharashtra achieves target of 112 runs to seal Ranji Trophy win","headline_hi":"महाराष्ट्र ने रणजी ट्रॉफी जीत पक्की करने के लिए 112 रनों का लक्ष्य हासिल किया","payload_en":{"story_id":61818,"headline":"Maharashtra achieves target of 112 runs to seal Ranji Trophy win","counts":{"articles":2,"independent_sources":1,"outlets":1},"has_established":false,"qualified_by":"express","perspective_mode":"none","perspectives":{"–":["The Hindu"]},"framing":[],"suicide":false,"thread":25963,"parents":[{"story_id":25963,"headline":"Bengal defeats Delhi by nine wickets in Ranji Trophy match"}],"children":[],"written_at":"2026-11-05T23:11:08","category":{"v":2,"primary":["india"],"secondary":["life"],"tertiary":["sport-films"]},"places":["maharashtra","west-bengal"],"people":["Tanay Sanghavi","Pradeep Dadhe","Seamer Dadhe","Abhimanyu Easwaran","Abishek Porel","Ankur Paul","Hitesh Walunj","Mohammed Shami"],"narrative":{"paragraphs":[[{"text":"On 5 November, Bengal suffered its first defeat of the season.","ids":[102325],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"On Wednesday, 4 November 2026, Mohammed Shami trapped Pradeep Dadhe in front in the fourth over of the day, and Abhimanyu Easwaran was caught behind in it.","ids":[102343,102346],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"On Wednesday, 4 November 2026, Tanay Sanghavi dismissed Sudip Gharami and Sudip Chatterjee in the ninth over.","ids":[102349],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"On Wednesday, 4 November 2026, only 28 overs were bowled in three hours and 16 minutes of play.","ids":[102350],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"On Thursday, 5 November 2026, Maharashtra achieved the target of 112 runs, is in first place on the table with 19 points, and this was its biggest win of the season.","ids":[102315,102322,102324],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Ankur Paul was caught at silly point off Hitesh Walunj after tea.","ids":[102353],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"On Thursday, Maharashtra defeated Bengal by 10 wickets in a Ranji Trophy Elite Group-C cricket match, and Abishek Porel scored 65 runs and Sumanta Gupta scored 59 runs for Bengal.","ids":[102311,102332],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"A 60-run 10th wicket stand between Dadhe and Sanghavi ended, and Sanghavi scored 60 not out off 179 balls with three fours and one six, while Sachin Dhas scored 61 runs not out in 68 balls with 10 fours, and Prithvi Shaw scored 53 runs not out in 50 balls with 3 fours and 4 sixes.","ids":[102351,102362,102328,102330],"class":"single","sources":[1,2]}],[{"text":"On 4 November, Bengal scored 76 for four wickets in 24 overs in their second innings, a figure later updated when Bengal's second innings total reached 186 runs in 54.4 overs.","ids":[102364,102334],"class":"single","sources":[1,2]},{"text":"Maharashtra scored 218 in their first innings in 82.5 overs, and its second innings total was 114 runs for no loss in 19.4 overs.","ids":[102363,102335],"class":"single","sources":[1,2]}]],"section_keys":["news","happened","happened","happened","happened","performers","performers","numbers"],"sources":[{"n":1,"url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","outlet":"The Hindu","title":"Ranji Trophy: Maharashtra coasts to  biggest win of the season against Bengal","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true},{"n":2,"url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-rain-holds-centrestage-as-bengal-scrambles-to-save-the-match-against-maharashtra/article71665453.ece","outlet":"The Hindu","title":"Ranji Trophy: Rain holds centrestage as Bengal scrambles to save the match against Maharashtra","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true}],"other_coverage":[{"text":"Bad light and rain affected the play on the penultimate day of the match.","ids":[102365],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"The weather conditions were described as favourable for Bengal.","ids":[102366],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"Maharashtra pacers bowled wicket-to-wicket in overcast conditions.","ids":[102367],"class":"single","sources":[2]}]},"timeline":[],"undated":[],"established":[],"contested":[{"text":"Bengal scored 143 in its first innings.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"},{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-rain-holds-centrestage-as-bengal-scrambles-to-save-the-match-against-maharashtra/article71665453.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Maharashtra defeated Bengal by 10 wickets in a Ranji Trophy Elite Group-C cricket match.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Maharashtra achieved the target of 112 runs.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Seamer Dadhe dismissed Suraj Jaiswal and Shahbaz Ahmed via leg before wicket.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Left-arm spinner Hitesh Walunj dismissed Abishek Porel.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Maharashtra is in first place on the table with 19 points.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"This was Maharashtra's biggest win of the season.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"This was Bengal's first defeat of the season.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Sachin Dhas scored 61 runs not out in 68 balls with 10 fours.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Prithvi Shaw scored 53 runs not out in 50 balls with 3 fours and 4 sixes.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Abishek Porel scored 65 runs and Sumanta Gupta scored 59 runs for Bengal.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ranji-trophy-maharashtra-coasts-to-biggest-win-of-the-season-against-bengal/article71669359.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Bengal's second innings total was 186 runs in 54.4 overs.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hin